[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 14: 4-PAM and its eye.
# 4-PAM sends two bits per symbol on the I axis only, with four Gray-labelled amplitudes. Open the Eye tab and the In-phase component: three stacked eyes appear, one between each pair of levels. Each eye is smaller than the single eye of BPSK, so 4-PAM needs more SNR for the same error rate. The Q trace stays at zero.
Version=2
Modulation=4-PAM
NumberOfSymbols=1024
SymbolRateBaud=1000
SamplesPerSymbol=8
Pulse=RRC
RRCBeta=0.2
SpanSymbols=10
AmplitudeGain=1
DataSource=Random
Seed=5489
Bits=
NoiseSampleCount=2048
NoiseSampleRateHz=8000
NoisePower=1
AwgnEnabled=true
AwgnSnrDb=22
NoiseSeed=5490
